From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eugene Feinberg <uge@persimmons.ai>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 12:48:07 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 07/37] LLHD Sig2Reg: name the narrowed drive and its kind
 under LLVM_DEBUG

There was no way to answer 'which modules does each narrowing rule actually
fire in', which is the first question a correctness check has to answer --
picking modules to verify by grepping the RTL for a signal name got the
attribution wrong twice. This prints the enclosing module, the signal, the
range count, and WHICH of the three feeder shapes matched.

Run it with --mlir-disable-threading: the module pass runs in parallel and
the debug stream interleaves into unparseable garbage without it (an earlier
tally taken with threading on reported 98 narrowings, all one kind; the real
answer is 588 across three).

On OpenC910: 249 combinational, 319 next, 20 reset-value, over 65 modules.
---
 lib/Dialect/LLHD/Transforms/Sig2RegPass.cpp | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lib/Dialect/LLHD/Transforms/Sig2RegPass.cpp b/lib/Dialect/LLHD/Transforms/Sig2RegPass.cpp
index 3617e4172..7df031d73 100644
--- a/lib/Dialect/LLHD/Transforms/Sig2RegPass.cpp
+++ b/lib/Dialect/LLHD/Transforms/Sig2RegPass.cpp
@@ -462,6 +462,24 @@ public:
                       selfFeedback = firregOp.getResult();
                     }
                     auto narrowed = tryNarrowFeeder(feeder, sigOp, selfFeedback);
+                    LLVM_DEBUG({
+                      if (narrowed) {
+                        auto parent =
+                            sigOp->getParentOfType<hw::HWModuleOp>();
+                        llvm::dbgs()
+                            << "  - narrowed "
+                            << (!firregOp ? "combinational"
+                                          : (firregOp.getNext() ==
+                                                     firregOp.getResult() &&
+                                             firregOp.getResetValue()
+                                                 ? "reset-value"
+                                                 : "next"))
+                            << " drive of @"
+                            << (parent ? parent.getModuleName() : "?") << "."
+                            << sigOp.getName().value_or("?") << " to "
+                            << narrowed->size() << " range(s)\n";
+                      }
+                    });
                     if (narrowed) {
                       bool isArray = isa<hw::ArrayType>(driveOp.getValue().getType());
                       auto arrayTy = isArray ? cast<hw::ArrayType>(
